  "reason": "No experiments have been completed, so there is no evidence to exploit and maximum uncertainty across all design axes. The most informative first experiment is a minimal, well-understood baseline that establishes a reference performance level. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest configuration in the space: PCA is a standard, low-risk dimensionality reduction; singleprofile avoids aggregation complexity; and no image or fusion components are involved. This gives a clean RNA-only reference that will be essential for later determining whether (a) learned RNA encoders (scvi, scgpt) add value, (b) multiprofile aggregation helps, and (c) multimodal fusion actually improves over the single-modality baseline. Starting here reduces the risk of confounding implementation issues with design effects and anchors all subsequent comparisons."
}

